    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$5521.47$, using 14% depreciation p.a.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Percentage change}&=\\frac{\\text{Change}}{\\text{Original}}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage change}&=\\frac{18\\,453.02-21\\,457}{21\\,457}\\times100\\%\\\\\\text{Percentage change}&=-14\\%\\end{align*}$$\nThe value decreases by 14% each year, so $r=0.14$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=V_0(1-r)^n\\\\S&=24\\,950(1-0.14)^{10}\\\\S&\\approx\\$5521.47\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
